  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kandukuri Babu vs State Of Ap on 17 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.4952 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/accused seeks to quash the proceedings against him in P.R.C. No.40 of 2019 on the file of Additional Junior Civil Judge, Badvel, YSR Kadapa District, which was taken cognizance for the offences under Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 and Sections 57, 58 r/w 26, 30 of Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 10.07.2019 at about 11.00 a.m., when the complainant along with his staff, on credible information rushed to backside of Poleramma temple, Mydurkur road, Badvel Town, found the accused holding two cloth bags of banned tobacco products and hence, arrested the accused and seized the same and registered a case in Crime No.207 of 2019 of Badvel Urban Police Station, for the offences stated supra.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
